WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.457
Case expressions and filter are two ways to perform conditional aggregation.

00:00:05.457 --> 00:00:10.532
The case expression is flexible and works in many database systems.

00:00:10.532 --> 00:00:18.517
The filter clause is especially easy to read in Postgres when we create category specific counts or sums.

00:00:18.517 --> 00:00:22.597
The more important issue is not which syntax looks better.

00:00:22.597 --> 00:00:29.693
The important issue is whether the output grain, category conditions, and aggregation rule are correct.
